# Qwen3.6-27B, QuantTrio AWQ INT4 (AutoAWQ GEMM, group 128, zero point; attention q/k/v, DeltaNet
# in_proj_a/b, layer 0, the MTP head and the vision tower stay bf16; AWQ-Marlin). The config
# declares float16; the preset serves bf16 activations.
# Its weights (19.05 GiB) leave 0.62 GiB of KV cache at 0.95 of the GPU, short of the 0.81 GiB one
# 8,192-token request needs, so this preset takes 0.97 and halves --max-num-batched-tokens to 512
# (less activation memory, half the echo prompt-logprob spike in the smaller headroom).
# Measured on an RTX 3090 (docs/research/candidates.md): 19.05 GiB weights, 1.14 GiB KV cache
# (11,083 tokens), ~125 s to healthy.
# Shared by the Qwen3.5-architecture candidate presets (docs/research/candidates.md): thinking off for every
# chat and /tokenize render (the template thinks by default); --language-model-only skips the
# vision tower; bf16 activations (the base model's dtype); --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 bounds
# echo's prompt-logprob spike (full 248k-vocab logits per prompt token of a chunk, not covered by
# vLLM's startup memory profile); --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling defaults.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=QuantTrio/Qwen3.6-27B-AWQ
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=9b507bdc9afafb87b7898700cc2a591aa6639461
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.97
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking":false}'
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=512 --generation-config=vllm'
